.TH HARNESS 1 "September 2026" "agent-harness 0.1.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
harness \- performance layer for coding agents
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B harness
[\fICOMMAND\fR] [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Skills, instincts, memory, security and research-first that works the same
in Claude Code, Codex, Opencode, Cursor, Kiro CLI and Kiro.
.PP
Run \fBharness init\fR in your project, then \fBharness doctor\fR to verify.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B init [--harness <name>] [--auto] [--migrate]
Set up harness in current project.
.TP
.B doctor [--fix]
Check adapters, skills, security.
.TP
.B bench [--quick]
Run performance checks.
.TP
.B skill <add|list|remove|search|info> [name]
Manage skills.
.TP
.B memory <sync|show|edit|prune>
Manage persistent memory.
.TP
.B research <query> [--plan]
Research-first capture with citations.
.TP
.B security <audit|scan|fix>
Security checks.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR https://github.com/TheElephantCoder/agent-harness
